+**Builder-comparison rounds.** When the Status lines say the active round compares builders, a builder dispatch adds these steps; the plan's round section defines each term. After `profile` and before choosing, run `enroll` with your eligibility decision: both arms acceptable under [model selection](../../../docs/model-selection.md), and the round's review route fits the task. Dispatch the arm it prints, or choose as usual when it reports the task not enrolled. If `enroll` fails or its result is unclear, run it again for the same task ID; only `status --task-id` showing no record makes the task not enrolled. During the episode, run `review` when the first review completes, `repair` at each resubmission after a review that required changes, `pause` at once on any P1 against a Terra-arm build, and `close` at the end (`withdraw` if it was never dispatched). Do not tell the reviewer of an enrolled episode which model built it.
+
+<!-- cli-synopsis script=metrics/scripts/task_profile_record.py subs="start profile assign attribute enroll review repair close pause status" display="python3 -I metrics/scripts/task_profile_record.py" -->
